+// zc != NULL: leading all-zero chunks per row. want_lu: returns the end of the unmasked columns of rows
+// [q_start, q_start + n_rows_q) in 64-column chunks (0 when every value is masked), else 0.
+// MSCAN result cache: the FA ops of one op batch (e.g. every attention layer of a prefill graph) read the same
+// broadcast mask, so the per-query-block scan results (lu_cols, zero chunks per row, last unmasked chunk per row)
+// are the same for each of them. Entries are keyed by the mask rows address, row stride, nek1, rows and scan mode
+// and are valid only within the op batch and graph that wrote them (htp_fa_mscan_gen is bumped at every batch start
